    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "DOUGLAS\nDC-3\nPASSENGER BRIEFING CARD\nNOTE: THIS CARD CONTAINS IMPORTANT\nINFORMATION. PLEASE READ BEFORE TAKEOFF.\n• OBSERVE \"NO SMOKING\" \u0026 \"FASTEN SEAT BELT\" SIGNS\n• NO SMOKING IN LAVATORY.\n884\nEMERGENCY INFORMATION\nWINDOW EXITS\n1. REMOVE CELLULOID COVER\nAND TURN HANDLE\nCLOCKWISE AS SHOWN.\n2. PUSH WINDOW\nOUTWARD.\nWINDOW EXIT\nWINDOW EXIT\n3. STEP THROUGH WINDOW.\nSIT AND SLIDE OFF WING\nVINDOW EXIT\nMAIN CABIN DOOR\n1. GRASP HANDLE AND\nTURN CLOCKWISE\n2. PUSH DOOR OUTWARD.\nCABIN\nDOOR\nEXIT\nFLOTATION EQUIPMENT\nTHE DC-3 IS EQUIPPED WITH EITHER LIFE VESTS OR FLOTATION CUSHIONS\nLIFE VESTS\nOR\nLIFE VESTS LOCATED BENEATH SEAT.\nDONNING INSTRUCTIONS ON VEST.\n-OR\nFLOTATION CUSHIONS\n1. LIFT UP AT REAR OF CUSHION.\n2. PUSH DOWN ON FRONT TO UNHOOK.\n3. USE STRAPS FOR HOLDING.",
      "SEAT BELTS\n1. SEAT BELT MUST BE FASTENED\nFOR TAKEOFF AND LANDING\n2. FOR OTHER PHASES OF FLIGHT, PLEASE\nKEEP SEAT BELT FASTENED.\nPULL TO\nTIGHTEN\nPULL TO\nRELEASE\nPROCEDURES FOR\nEMERGENCY LANDING\n1. ADJUST YOUR SEAT BACK TO UPRIGHT\nPOSITION.\n2. NO SMOKING. REMOVE OBJECTS THAT MAY\nHURT YOU SUCH AS GLASSES, PENS, ETC\n3. FASTEN YOUR SEAT BELT AND TAKE THE\nPOSITION INDICATED BY FIGURE\n4. AFTER AIRCRAFT HAS STOPPED, UNFASTEN\nYOUR SEAT BELT AND PROCEED TO NEAREST\nEXIT AS INDICATED BY THE CREW.\nPORTABLE ELECTRONIC DEVICES\nARE YOU CARRYING A PORTABLE RADIO OR RECORDER? FEDERAL AVIATION\nAGENCY (FAA) REGULATION PROHIBITS THE OPERATION IN-FLIGHT OF CERTAIN\nPORTABLE ELECTRONIC DEVICES SINCE THEY CAN INTERFERE WITH THE\nAIRCRAFT'S NAVIGATION SYSTEM. PLEASE CHECK WITH THE FLIGHT ATTENDANT\nBEFORE OPERATING YOUR RADIO, DICTATING MACHINE OR RECORDER.\nPLEASE DO NOT REMOVE THIS CARD\nFROM AIRCRAFT\nAmerica's Oldest Regional Airline\nA"
    ],
